entry at order 1. Lower pluck arpeggios one octave and soften their level; pipe retains full phrase/bends with no patch vibrato and a softer attack. Quiet root-following pad breaths on channel 7 in patterns 0/1/8. Order, tempo, speed and B01 loop retained. Original Breach Vector retained.") ("codex" "2026-09-21" "Listening revision III: raise the muted FM riff default and explicit accent volumes by 12 percent (rounded tracker levels). Preserve every note, gate, effect, instrument patch, other channel and arrangement from II. David liked the smoother sound but wanted the riff a little more audible. Original II retained.") ("codex" "2026-09-21" "Listening revision IV: lift instrument 4, the FM bass/synth present from the opening, by 15 percent in default and explicit tracker levels (48 to 55, 40 to 46). Preserve its patch and phrasing, the later grit bass levels, and the muted riff lift from III. David wants a little more supporting presence, not a foreground lead. All earlier versions retained.") ("codex" "2026-09-21" "Calm/tense arrangement based on accepted breach-vector-v4. calm: order 0-15; transition: 16; tense: 17-35; B11 loops the tense region. Calm preserves source phrases and patches; new tense variants and a dedicated transition retain the original clock. Separate calm/tense loop sources are generated by render.py. Accepted full reference retained.") ("m1 (marks from the documented layout)" "2026-09-21" "set marks calm: 0 fill: 16 tense: 17"))))
